in 2015 pole star became the official  performance division of Volvo cars the  collaboration with the Swedish automaker  actually goes back to 1996 when pole  star was founded under the name flash  engineering it's been Volvo's  Motorsports partner ever since now it  has designed the most powerful  production Mobile's  of all time the pole star branded s60  sedan and the v60 station wagon  back in 2009 Polestar began supplying  tuning and performance accessories for  road going Volvo's the new dynamic duo  boasts over 50 optimizations resulting  in 270 kilowatts of output and an  equipment package that translates into a  sports car for everyday driving  we checked out the s60 sedan powered by  a souped-up t6 gasoline engine and  all-wheel drive this Polestar production  model comes with plenty of Motorsports  caliber and provides the technical basis  for the current Volvo racing cars and  the FIA World Touring Car Championship  which Volvo returned to last year our  car reviewer Michelle Assenmacher finds  the s60 promising from the outside  thanks to its beefy looks our first  impression on the inside however is the  very opposite the center console with  its maze of buttons and knobs is not too  user-friendly the interior features pole  stars stylish blue stitching among the  other nice features a heated steering  wheel and carbon fiber inlays adorning  the dashboard and center console  the sports seats with their new buck and  nappa leather upholstery provides solid  support for more aggressive driving  styles michelle admits she kind of fell  in love with the steering wheel that  combination of smooth leather and  alcantara gives the wheel far better  grip and a gorgeous feel the suspension  comes with shock absorbers that can be  adjusted and a variety of settings from  super comfortable to super hard ideal  for taking the car out on the racetrack  for example for everyday use the mid  range setting makes the most sense  the s60 also has the power to take on  the steepest of mountains in style  Michelle explains Michelle only found it  right to put the most powerful Volvo  ever through its paces on the Autobahn  as well even at high speeds she feels  that customary Volvo safety so for now  we have the mid-sized s and v60 editions  but Volvo intends to establish Polestar  as a performance brand for other  segments as well it will be interesting  to see which models bear the pole star  badge in the future  the show has to hand it to the s60  Polestar on one front it's a lot of fun  off the highway as well good  acceleration of these curvy country  roads and a tight turning circle testify  to the cars agility a pleasure to drive  all in all the Volvo s60 Polestar is a  sporty ride that's really fun to drive  all twist the net successfully on touch  me ohonta mystic v whatever lights it  prices for the s60 Polestar in germany  started 68,000 euros
 

